00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:37.340
just a young couple that was moving.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:38.790
They were in the process of trying to move

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:42.960
from New Jersey to California in a van.

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:45.710
And they were like, these fires started.

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:48.030
And so where we were gonna go

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:49.430
is basically on fire right now.

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:53.363
So we're kind of just hanging
out, this was in Nevada.

00:21:54.490 --> 00:21:55.610
And they had been on the
road for like three weeks

00:21:55.610 --> 00:21:57.210
and he was completely clean shaven

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:58.320
and I haven't thought about that at all.

00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:00.950
And he was not the kind of
man who can't grow a beard.

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:02.600
I could see the potential for a beard.

00:22:02.600 --> 00:22:03.433
I think he was--

00:22:03.433 --> 00:22:04.630
He was just a shaver.

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:06.870
He had his destination in mind

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:08.210
and I think it's psychological.

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:10.160
It's like, you know what, for that guy,

00:22:11.340 --> 00:22:12.240
I'm putting a lot on him.

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:16.850
But I think, his tie
to the civilized world

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:18.350
is him continuing to shave.

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:19.640
And once he stopped shaving,

00:22:19.640 --> 00:22:22.840
he was giving up on his
hope of ever reconnecting

00:22:22.840 --> 00:22:24.470
with society on the west coast

00:22:24.470 --> 00:22:26.230
where he was gonna make a life for himself

00:22:26.230 --> 00:22:28.190
and I presume his partner.

00:22:28.190 --> 00:22:29.560
Yeah and the hashtag van life.

00:22:29.560 --> 00:22:32.430
And they were like take,

00:22:32.430 --> 00:22:36.640
they were in a converted Astro,
a four wheel drive Astro.

00:22:36.640 --> 00:22:37.630
No judgement.

00:22:37.630 --> 00:22:39.890
And that had a popup thing on it.

00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:44.313
And I could tell by
the way that the woman,

00:22:45.750 --> 00:22:49.710
his companion was taking
pictures of like this hot spring

00:22:49.710 --> 00:22:52.440
that we were at and everything
and waiting for the sunset.

00:22:52.440 --> 00:22:55.910
And she went to the hot spring
and she moved things around.

00:22:55.910 --> 00:22:58.420
I was like, this is a
total hashtag van life.

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:00.170
And like, they're getting
these really good pictures.

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:02.950
I can only imagine what this
Instagram is gonna look like.

00:23:02.950 --> 00:23:07.950
Well, our van was, everything was,

00:23:08.420 --> 00:23:09.760
it had all the amenities,

00:23:09.760 --> 00:23:12.270
but the materials that they
used to make everything

00:23:12.270 --> 00:23:13.230
were very rugged.

00:23:13.230 --> 00:23:15.210
It felt like you could just take a hose

00:23:15.210 --> 00:23:17.010
and hose everything off..

00:23:17.010 --> 00:23:19.710
Because it's a rental and I mean,

00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:23.550
they touted how much they
rigorously clean the thing.

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:25.850
In between people using it.

00:23:25.850 --> 00:23:27.440
If you were to do your own deal,

00:23:27.440 --> 00:23:29.600
you would want like
mahogany, what do you--

00:23:29.600 --> 00:23:32.010
Yeah, the ones, it wasn't picturesque

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:34.640
because you start to think
about hashtag van life

00:23:34.640 --> 00:23:36.750
is these people who
put stuff on Instagram.

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:39.260
And I was sitting in the
back of the van on our,

00:23:39.260 --> 00:23:41.450
the day after Zion, when we were like,

00:23:41.450 --> 00:23:43.000
we're just gonna take this day.

00:23:43.910 --> 00:23:45.930
We're not gonna rush off
the, we're gonna wake up,

00:23:45.930 --> 00:23:48.310
we're gonna eat breakfast,
we're gonna hang out here.

00:23:48.310 --> 00:23:51.100
Hell, We may even take
a nap before lunchtime--

00:23:51.100 --> 00:23:52.290
A late morning nap.

00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:53.953
Yeah, which we did.

00:23:55.180 --> 00:23:57.010
Yeah, never been done before.

00:23:57.010 --> 00:23:57.980
And then I was like, you know what?--

00:23:57.980 --> 00:23:59.020
That seems almost impossible.

00:23:59.020 --> 00:23:59.947
Before--

00:24:00.900 --> 00:24:01.733
Yeah, I know, right?

00:24:01.733 --> 00:24:03.730
The whole hanging around in the morning,

00:24:03.730 --> 00:24:05.870
which for me ended up being the highlight.

00:24:05.870 --> 00:24:06.870
I'll talk about that,

00:24:06.870 --> 00:24:10.070
but never did it strike me that

00:24:10.070 --> 00:24:12.770
I should get back in
the tent and take a nap.

00:24:12.770 --> 00:24:13.940
Like not even--

00:24:13.940 --> 00:24:15.580
Well these are, it's different.

00:24:15.580 --> 00:24:17.780
The back doors of the van are open.

00:24:17.780 --> 00:24:19.450
This is a hashtag van life moment.

00:24:19.450 --> 00:24:21.700
You lay down in the bed

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:25.000
and then you stand up towards
the cab at the driver's seat.

00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:27.900
And someone takes a photo
through the back of the van

00:24:27.900 --> 00:24:28.999
at the scenery someone's--

00:24:28.999 --> 00:24:29.832
Did you take a bunch of photos

00:24:29.832 --> 00:24:31.180
that you're gonna post hashtag van life?

00:24:31.180 --> 00:24:32.013
Well, I said,

00:24:32.013 --> 00:24:34.270
"Christy, come in here
and take a picture of me."

00:24:34.270 --> 00:24:36.760
I was laying on the bed thinking
about maybe taking a nap.

00:24:36.760 --> 00:24:38.320
She was outside reading a book.

00:24:38.320 --> 00:24:40.180
And I was like, "Come in
here, take a picture."

00:24:40.180 --> 00:24:42.330
And so she takes my phone
and she comes right up to me.

00:24:42.330 --> 00:24:43.322
I was like, "No, no, no.

00:24:43.322 --> 00:24:46.743
"Haven't you seen go back to the cab,

00:24:46.743 --> 00:24:48.250
"you wanna shoot past me."

00:24:48.250 --> 00:24:49.710
And then we try to do that.

00:24:49.710 --> 00:24:51.468
And then I looked at the
pictures and I was like,

00:24:51.468 --> 00:24:53.663
you know what I'm not gonna
blame Christy for this.

00:24:54.530 --> 00:24:56.290
It's the decor, it's the light,

00:24:56.290 --> 00:24:57.970
so many things have to line up

00:24:57.970 --> 00:25:00.830
for it to be hashtaggable van life.

00:25:00.830 --> 00:25:03.650
And let me tell you, it was not worth it

00:25:03.650 --> 00:25:05.145
because that right there--

00:25:05.145 --> 00:25:06.343
I think it ruins the enjoyment.

00:25:07.230 --> 00:25:10.040
It proved to me how much of a,

00:25:10.040 --> 00:25:12.270
if you get really good at it
you can probably do it quickly,

00:25:12.270 --> 00:25:13.680
but it takes a lot of practice

00:25:13.680 --> 00:25:15.530
to look like you're cool out there.

00:25:15.530 --> 00:25:17.010
When this woman--
Van life in it.

00:25:17.010 --> 00:25:18.840
This woman went to the hot spring,

00:25:18.840 --> 00:25:21.721
she just moved a bunch of
stuff around the hot spring.

00:25:21.721 --> 00:25:23.470
And then started taking pictures.

00:25:23.470 --> 00:25:25.860
No, I was, I'll explain why,

00:25:25.860 --> 00:25:27.570
but I was very close to the hot spring.

00:25:27.570 --> 00:25:29.830
The thing that I didn't fully anticipate,

00:25:29.830 --> 00:25:30.990
I guess I could have known this,

00:25:30.990 --> 00:25:32.930
but it's one thing to say
it, it's another thing,

00:25:32.930 --> 00:25:34.120
it's kinda like going to a park.

00:25:34.120 --> 00:25:36.220
You can say how beautiful it
is, but until you're there,

00:25:36.220 --> 00:25:37.460
you really can't experience it.

00:25:37.460 --> 00:25:40.770
I think in a similar way, I could've known

00:25:40.770 --> 00:25:42.650
that this camping excursion

00:25:42.650 --> 00:25:43.980
would have been unlike any other,

00:25:43.980 --> 00:25:47.090
but I really didn't think it
through until it was happening.

00:25:47.090 --> 00:25:51.380
First of all, me and Christy,
the best of my recollection,

00:25:51.380 --> 00:25:53.790
we've never gone camping
just the two of us.

00:25:53.790 --> 00:25:55.740
Yeah me and Jesie have never done it.

00:25:56.810 --> 00:25:59.220
Every time that I would go camping.

00:25:59.220 --> 00:26:00.757
I mean, in college we would go

00:26:00.757 --> 00:26:03.070
and it was also mission oriented.

00:26:03.070 --> 00:26:05.810
We're gonna go to this place
so that we can experience

00:26:05.810 --> 00:26:09.080
these things so that
we can do these things.

00:26:09.080 --> 00:26:14.070
And whenever we would
start going off-roading,

00:26:14.070 --> 00:26:15.540
like when we first moved
out here and we're like,

00:26:15.540 --> 00:26:18.240
we did the Death Valley
trips and stuff like that,

00:26:18.240 --> 00:26:21.250
camping was kind of just
the means to bed down

00:26:21.250 --> 00:26:24.383
in between doing more
off-roading, you know?

00:26:25.530 --> 00:26:27.530
The most prevalent experience at camping

00:26:27.530 --> 00:26:29.210
is bringing the kids.

00:26:29.210 --> 00:26:31.360
And there's so much logistics associated

00:26:31.360 --> 00:26:34.600
with once you have one, two or three kids.

00:26:34.600 --> 00:26:35.950
Good gosh.

00:26:35.950 --> 00:26:37.150
Right, definitely one too many.

00:26:37.150 --> 00:26:39.970
And you know, it's just trying
to keep everybody straight

00:26:39.970 --> 00:26:41.710
and keep everything together.

00:26:41.710 --> 00:26:42.560
And somebody is all,

00:26:42.560 --> 00:26:45.563
everybody's opinions
and everybody's on edge.

00:26:46.500 --> 00:26:48.303
I didn't realize how,

00:26:49.900 --> 00:26:53.220
I came with a mentality of, this is not,

00:26:53.220 --> 00:26:55.250
everything we talked about
in the last Ear Biscuit

00:26:55.250 --> 00:26:56.820
it's not about,

00:26:56.820 --> 00:26:59.430
it's just about taking
every day as it comes.

00:26:59.430 --> 00:27:03.560
And as my desired outcome is
quality time with Christy.

00:27:03.560 --> 00:27:07.020
And then hopefully that this
is overall a great experience

00:27:07.020 --> 00:27:08.913
that we can then do again.

00:27:10.070 --> 00:27:13.173
So within that context,
I started to realize,

00:27:14.980 --> 00:27:17.120
I started to have thoughts
like the first night

00:27:17.120 --> 00:27:20.510
when we were camping and
setting up the campus so easy,

00:27:20.510 --> 00:27:22.000
there was no tent to set up.

00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:24.120
There was no fire to
start, which is illegal.

00:27:24.120 --> 00:27:26.420
I just had that propane tank.

00:27:26.420 --> 00:27:28.100
And you just fire that
up, cook some stuff,

00:27:28.100 --> 00:27:29.390
you immediately turn it off and on.

00:27:29.390 --> 00:27:32.860
And like, it doesn't spread
flames at all, it's legal.

00:27:32.860 --> 00:27:34.333
But it makes it so simple.

00:27:38.143 --> 00:27:40.230
I found myself having this--

00:27:40.230 --> 00:27:41.170
Abundance of time.

00:27:41.170 --> 00:27:46.170
Headspace to think and I
actually had the thought

00:27:47.220 --> 00:27:51.740
for the first time, I'm
starting to connect with nature.

00:27:51.740 --> 00:27:53.830
Like you hear people talking about

00:27:53.830 --> 00:27:55.609
how they go out into nature and like,

00:27:55.609 --> 00:27:56.442
some people say,

00:27:56.442 --> 00:27:58.730
"Well, I feel closest to
God when I'm in nature."

00:27:58.730 --> 00:28:02.620
Or I just like to connect with the earth.

00:28:02.620 --> 00:28:05.113
And I was like, you know,

00:28:06.060 --> 00:28:08.820
hunters do that in their own way.

00:28:08.820 --> 00:28:10.340
They connect with it so hard--

00:28:10.340 --> 00:28:11.173
So hard, so this--

00:28:11.173 --> 00:28:12.006
They kill it.

00:28:14.130 --> 00:28:17.360
But it's this like primal
thing, like farmers do it,

00:28:17.360 --> 00:28:18.310
they get their hands dirty.

00:28:18.310 --> 00:28:22.700
They like have a relationship
with the earth that they learn

00:28:22.700 --> 00:28:27.160
to speak its language and to
give to it and benefit from it.

00:28:27.160 --> 00:28:30.070
And I actually started
to having these thoughts,

00:28:30.070 --> 00:28:32.670
just like a level of
appreciation for connection,

00:28:32.670 --> 00:28:34.163
with nature that,

00:28:35.160 --> 00:28:37.930
on all of the campuses I've been through,

00:28:37.930 --> 00:28:40.763
there just wasn't a lot of space for that.

00:28:43.891 --> 00:28:45.780
And you know, we're like setting
up our camp, we're eating,

00:28:45.780 --> 00:28:47.247
we're watching the sun go down--

00:28:47.247 --> 00:28:50.800
And it also helps in,

00:28:50.800 --> 00:28:52.400
I'm assuming this was your experience.

00:28:52.400 --> 00:28:53.460
'Cause definitely my experience.

00:28:53.460 --> 00:28:55.880
It also helps for me when

00:28:55.880 --> 00:28:57.880
you're not in an established campground.

00:28:58.800 --> 00:29:00.250
To me that like--

00:29:00.250 --> 00:29:02.100
Dispersed camping for the win.

00:29:02.100 --> 00:29:04.580
That made all the difference in the world

00:29:04.580 --> 00:29:05.785
in being able to--

00:29:05.785 --> 00:29:06.710
Waiting for you to say for the win--

00:29:06.710 --> 00:29:11.020
To feel like there's an
opportunity to connect

00:29:12.700 --> 00:29:16.600
because when you're in this,
like, okay, well there's this,

00:29:16.600 --> 00:29:17.910
especially when it's like a pay--

00:29:17.910 --> 00:29:19.160
If you're at a campground.

00:29:19.160 --> 00:29:21.570
Campground and there's
a building over there

00:29:21.570 --> 00:29:24.413
that a person built that
you can take a crap in.

00:29:25.510 --> 00:29:28.160
That to me, that just takes away from it.

00:29:28.160 --> 00:29:30.310
Even if the scenery is
beautiful and then also,

00:29:30.310 --> 00:29:33.380
oh and there's another person
right there next to you

00:29:33.380 --> 00:29:35.180
and you can hear their conversation.

00:29:35.180 --> 00:29:36.510
You can like hear,

00:29:36.510 --> 00:29:37.990
even if you can't make
out what they're saying,

00:29:37.990 --> 00:29:39.173
you can kinda just hear

00:29:41.848 --> 00:29:42.681
You can't stand that.
And it's like,

00:29:42.681 --> 00:29:44.460
okay, that's part of camping
is what we've thought.

00:29:44.460 --> 00:29:46.570
And we have camp like totally isolated,

00:29:46.570 --> 00:29:48.360
but we've done it with other people.

00:29:48.360 --> 00:29:50.800
Like when we went to Death
Valley, there was nobody around,

00:29:50.800 --> 00:29:52.780
in many of those nights
except for the group.

00:29:52.780 --> 00:29:55.613
But it was like five trucks full of guys.

00:29:56.590 --> 00:29:57.580
So you still have that.

00:29:57.580 --> 00:30:01.040
There's no isolation, but yeah
definitely that first night

00:30:01.040 --> 00:30:05.540
we found this amazing campsite
just outside of Zion on

00:30:07.540 --> 00:30:11.510
national forest land
using the ioverlander app.

00:30:11.510 --> 00:30:13.320
That was the app that worked best for me.

00:30:13.320 --> 00:30:14.770
I ended up using that yeah.

00:30:14.770 --> 00:30:18.350
We didn't have cell service,
but the spot was so good.

00:30:18.350 --> 00:30:20.050
We were like, all right,
we're going to Zion tomorrow.

00:30:20.050 --> 00:30:23.170
We're gonna come back to the
same spot and enjoy it again

00:30:23.170 --> 00:30:24.800
because it's such a good spot.

00:30:24.800 --> 00:30:26.370
Like we could see the sunset,

00:30:26.370 --> 00:30:29.282
there was like a ravine right
there, there were red rocks.

00:30:29.282 --> 00:30:30.115
It was amazing.

00:30:30.115 --> 00:30:34.573
I took a Garmin satellite phone.

00:30:35.470 --> 00:30:36.303
Not a sponsor.

00:30:36.303 --> 00:30:38.850
I think it was the enrich
or something like that.

00:30:38.850 --> 00:30:41.350
And so even when I
didn't have cell service,

00:30:41.350 --> 00:30:43.630
I could text Jessie and it texts her

00:30:44.767 --> 00:30:45.900
and she gets a text on her phone--

00:30:45.900 --> 00:30:46.733
And a location.

00:30:46.733 --> 00:30:48.644
And a link to my location on the map.

00:30:48.644 --> 00:30:50.966
Oh, that's cool, I'll get one of those.

00:30:50.966 --> 00:30:52.210
And it's like a monthly service

00:30:52.210 --> 00:30:54.430
that you can turn on and off.

00:30:54.430 --> 00:30:56.330
And I think it was like
30 bucks for the month.

00:30:56.330 --> 00:30:57.163
And then you just turn it off

00:30:57.163 --> 00:30:59.160
and it's stagnant while
you're not using it.

00:30:59.160 --> 00:31:00.603
That's nice peace of mind because yeah--

00:31:00.603 --> 00:31:02.310
I mean, I was by myself.

00:31:02.310 --> 00:31:03.321
Yeah, so--

00:31:03.321 --> 00:31:06.100
I definitely had to do that.

00:31:06.100 --> 00:31:09.330
Yeah, so that isolation, it really creates

00:31:09.330 --> 00:31:11.650
so much more space than
I even anticipated.

00:31:11.650 --> 00:31:15.380
And it was just, it was relaxing

00:31:16.731 --> 00:31:19.040
and so it gets dark, you're hanging out

00:31:19.040 --> 00:31:21.710
and I turn off the,

00:31:21.710 --> 00:31:24.480
actually I didn't turn
off the propane fire yet.

00:31:24.480 --> 00:31:25.590
We were like sitting around the fire.

00:31:25.590 --> 00:31:27.927
We were looking up at
where we were just like,

00:31:27.927 --> 00:31:31.560
"Man, look at the stars."

00:31:31.560 --> 00:31:32.550
Oh yeah.

00:31:32.550 --> 00:31:33.940
It was it's the time of year,

00:31:33.940 --> 00:31:36.100
it took me a while to figure out why,

00:31:36.100 --> 00:31:37.560
I mean, it was totally clear.

00:31:37.560 --> 00:31:41.350
The most stars I had ever seen except for

00:31:41.350 --> 00:31:45.390
that night that we landed
in Fiji and it was dark.

00:31:45.390 --> 00:31:47.790
And we got on a boat
that had no lights on it.

00:31:47.790 --> 00:31:49.650
And they took us out to that Island

00:31:49.650 --> 00:31:51.170
that we stayed out for a week.

00:31:51.170 --> 00:31:54.280
And we looked up at the
sky on this boat which,

00:31:54.280 --> 00:31:56.587
Christy and I were talking
about that and we were like,

00:31:56.587 --> 00:31:57.770
"I can't believe we did that."

00:31:57.770 --> 00:31:58.990
Like in the middle of the night,

00:31:58.990 --> 00:32:00.280
it felt like in the pitch dark,

00:32:00.280 --> 00:32:02.900
we get on this boat and
then we're just going out

00:32:02.900 --> 00:32:05.390
and there's no lights on
the boat it seemed like

00:32:05.390 --> 00:32:09.830
because we would look up and
we saw so many stars that,

00:32:09.830 --> 00:32:11.990
and it took me back there because

00:32:13.150 --> 00:32:14.530
that was the only time
I'd seen as many stars

00:32:14.530 --> 00:32:15.500
as we saw that night.

00:32:15.500 --> 00:32:18.120
And I turn off the fire

00:32:18.120 --> 00:32:21.870
and I turn off all the lights on the van

00:32:21.870 --> 00:32:26.870
and we just craned our necks and just,

00:32:27.810 --> 00:32:28.950
we watched the stars

00:32:28.950 --> 00:32:32.393
like we were watching a movie
and that had never happened.

00:32:32.393 --> 00:32:37.230
And you can see like the bright light

00:32:38.100 --> 00:32:40.730
sort of like clusters
stars beyond the stars.

00:32:40.730 --> 00:32:42.540
I was like, is that the Milky Way?

00:32:42.540 --> 00:32:43.373
Well you're in the Milky Way.

00:32:43.373 --> 00:32:45.870
