Yeah, you can't be crowding people, man.

00:54:36.330 --> 00:54:37.990
It's a freaking desert,
there's all kinds of--

00:54:37.990 --> 00:54:42.990
Later on it's almost sunset this other man

00:54:43.590 --> 00:54:46.430
and it looked like his
teenage daughter came through

00:54:46.430 --> 00:54:49.710
and then they went up and
checked out the same spot.

00:54:49.710 --> 00:54:53.300
And then we're like watching
and we could see them.

00:54:54.183 --> 00:54:56.910
We could see and they got out of their car

00:54:56.910 --> 00:54:59.200
and they set up a tent and they stayed.

00:54:59.200 --> 00:55:00.130
So we were a little bit bound,

00:55:00.130 --> 00:55:02.810
but like we were facing the
other direction and they were on

00:55:02.810 --> 00:55:04.950
the other side of the van, like I said,

00:55:04.950 --> 00:55:06.350
200 yards away on another berm.

00:55:06.350 --> 00:55:09.940
So we still felt like we
had pretty good privacy.

00:55:09.940 --> 00:55:12.900
And then sun went down, we ate our dinner,

00:55:12.900 --> 00:55:14.483
it's nine o'clock at night.

00:55:15.560 --> 00:55:18.610
I'm inside washing the dishes,
she's outside on her phone.

00:55:18.610 --> 00:55:23.610
And all of a sudden I hear
gravel and I see like headlights

00:55:24.750 --> 00:55:26.620
hit the side of our van

00:55:26.620 --> 00:55:31.620
and a car is creeping up the dirt road

00:55:34.970 --> 00:55:35.937
coming right up to us.

00:55:35.937 --> 00:55:38.800
And like I'm in there washing.

00:55:38.800 --> 00:55:41.600
And the car comes past my field of view

00:55:41.600 --> 00:55:46.600
and stops where I can't see the car.

00:55:46.620 --> 00:55:48.710
I can't see who's driving
the car or anything.

00:55:48.710 --> 00:55:50.870
I can just see the tail of the car

00:55:50.870 --> 00:55:52.870
from where I was washing the dishes,

00:55:52.870 --> 00:55:54.130
but I could see Christy

00:55:54.130 --> 00:55:57.510
and she could see this car of course.

00:55:57.510 --> 00:55:59.810
'Cause she was out there in the open.

00:55:59.810 --> 00:56:02.840
And then the car stops--

00:56:02.840 --> 00:56:03.673
Right next to you.

00:56:03.673 --> 00:56:06.493
Right next to the back of our van.

00:56:07.770 --> 00:56:10.993
And I hear a guy say to Christy,

00:56:13.037 --> 00:56:15.057
"Are you selling any hot dogs?"

00:56:17.340 --> 00:56:21.710
And Christy said, and I freeze.

00:56:21.710 --> 00:56:22.543
And I'm like,

00:56:22.543 --> 00:56:25.460
"What the hell is this guy
asking about hot dogs?"

00:56:25.460 --> 00:56:26.770
And I'm like, I literally freeze

00:56:26.770 --> 00:56:27.670
and I'm like just listening.

00:56:27.670 --> 00:56:29.270
'Cause it was hard for me to hear.

00:56:29.270 --> 00:56:30.930
But my instinct was just to listen.

00:56:30.930 --> 00:56:34.457
So let me just, here's the exchange.

00:56:34.457 --> 00:56:36.760
"Are you selling any hot dogs?"

00:56:36.760 --> 00:56:38.210
And then I hear Christie say,

00:56:39.347 --> 00:56:42.747
"Nope, we actually don't have any."

00:56:44.350 --> 00:56:46.537
And then the guy says,

00:56:46.537 --> 00:56:48.853
"I'm going around getting people to vote,

00:56:50.407 --> 00:56:54.187
"vote on my pictures, to see
which ones they like best."

00:56:55.120 --> 00:56:58.163
And I'm still listening
and then Christy goes,

00:57:01.537 --> 00:57:03.980
"No, thank you, we're not interested."

00:57:03.980 --> 00:57:07.010
And she was like really
has a friendly voice.

00:57:07.010 --> 00:57:08.757
And then the guy said,

00:57:08.757 --> 00:57:11.687
"I just need you to vote on the photos.

00:57:11.687 --> 00:57:13.970
"See I have them right here."

00:57:13.970 --> 00:57:16.970
And I can't see him and then Christie--

00:57:16.970 --> 00:57:17.803
Hold on and you're still--

00:57:17.803 --> 00:57:18.636
Christy stood up.

00:57:18.636 --> 00:57:20.280
You're still in the kitchen?

00:57:20.280 --> 00:57:21.900
I'm still in the kitchen frozen.

00:57:21.900 --> 00:57:25.590
Like washing, like you gotta
be out there at this point.

00:57:25.590 --> 00:57:28.150
In retrospect I was
trying to figure out why,

00:57:28.150 --> 00:57:29.840
it was a frightened?

00:57:29.840 --> 00:57:31.810
Was I frozen with fear?

00:57:31.810 --> 00:57:33.793
Was I being strategic?

00:57:33.793 --> 00:57:34.626
Being strategic.

00:57:34.626 --> 00:57:35.590
I think all of these were having,

00:57:35.590 --> 00:57:37.270
because my initial thing was--

00:57:37.270 --> 00:57:38.663
The strategic hesitation.

00:57:40.890 --> 00:57:42.030
It's not basketball.

00:57:42.030 --> 00:57:46.260
I was trying to assess the
situation, I was freaked out.

00:57:46.260 --> 00:57:50.210
I was like, what the heck is going on?

00:57:50.210 --> 00:57:51.930
Like when the people came around earlier,

00:57:51.930 --> 00:57:54.480
I had come out and show my face.

00:57:54.480 --> 00:57:56.860
But my instincts told me to sit back here.

00:57:56.860 --> 00:58:00.010
Christy is gonna,

00:58:00.010 --> 00:58:02.830
I need to do whatever it takes
to deescalate the situation.

00:58:02.830 --> 00:58:04.626
This guy seems strange.

00:58:04.626 --> 00:58:07.044
A little.
Very strange.

00:58:07.044 --> 00:58:10.540
And I think I was just like,

00:58:10.540 --> 00:58:13.980
Christy is going to politely
get this guy to drive off.

00:58:13.980 --> 00:58:17.060
If I go out there and like say something,

00:58:17.060 --> 00:58:18.110
I might say the wrong,

00:58:18.110 --> 00:58:20.250
I had this instinct that I
was gonna say the wrong thing.

00:58:20.250 --> 00:58:22.120
And I will say--
You might escalate.

00:58:22.120 --> 00:58:24.050
I had had a couple, okay?

00:58:24.050 --> 00:58:24.883
Okay.

00:58:24.883 --> 00:58:29.740
So I wasn't, I was just
trying to know my limitations

00:58:31.060 --> 00:58:32.350
and I was like, I might go out there

00:58:32.350 --> 00:58:33.390
and I might be aggressive

00:58:33.390 --> 00:58:35.800
or I might try to scare
the guy, you know how I do.

00:58:35.800 --> 00:58:38.540
And that is your MO when you
enter into weird situations

00:58:38.540 --> 00:58:39.373
like that and you come in

00:58:39.373 --> 00:58:41.050
pretty aggressive and pretty strong.

00:58:42.461 --> 00:58:43.387
And if I had it, yeah, I escalate things.

00:58:44.425 --> 00:58:47.130
And if I've had a few, I speak louder.

00:58:47.130 --> 00:58:50.233
And so I think I didn't have enough that

00:58:50.233 --> 00:58:51.780
I didn't know that about myself.

00:58:51.780 --> 00:58:55.410
So my instinct told me
Christy's gonna deescalate this.

00:58:55.410 --> 00:58:58.130
I'm gonna stay back here
and then I can assess

00:58:58.130 --> 00:59:00.790
what I need to do when the time is right.

00:59:00.790 --> 00:59:04.403
So, I mean, he's like,

00:59:05.297 --> 00:59:08.197
"I'm going around getting
people to vote on my pictures,

00:59:08.197 --> 00:59:09.670
"to see which ones they like best."

00:59:09.670 --> 00:59:10.877
And then Christy's like,

00:59:10.877 --> 00:59:12.340
"No, thank you, we're not interested."

00:59:12.340 --> 00:59:13.647
And then he said,

00:59:13.647 --> 00:59:15.097
"I just need you to vote on the photos.

00:59:15.097 --> 00:59:16.320
"See I have them right here."

00:59:16.320 --> 00:59:18.280
And then Christie told me that he holds up

00:59:18.280 --> 00:59:20.470
like four by six photos.

00:59:20.470 --> 00:59:22.210
It wasn't on a phone,
it was literal photo.

00:59:22.210 --> 00:59:24.660
He had printed out photos and he was,

00:59:24.660 --> 00:59:25.730
of course he's in the driver's seat.

00:59:25.730 --> 00:59:27.360
He's leaning over the passenger seat,

00:59:27.360 --> 00:59:30.740
trying to lure Christy close to the car

00:59:30.740 --> 00:59:33.000
to show her the pictures.

00:59:33.000 --> 00:59:34.710
How old is this guy?

00:59:34.710 --> 00:59:35.543
What does he look?

00:59:35.543 --> 00:59:37.800
Christy said, it's very dark.

00:59:37.800 --> 00:59:39.193
Again, there's no moon.

00:59:40.361 --> 00:59:42.980
We had turned most of our lights off--

00:59:42.980 --> 00:59:44.180
You're way out there.

00:59:44.180 --> 00:59:46.360
We're way out there, yes.

00:59:46.360 --> 00:59:47.957
And Christy was like,

00:59:47.957 --> 00:59:52.247
"Ah, well, no, we're
just wrapping up dinner."

00:59:53.240 --> 00:59:57.320
And then she said she couldn't
see his face that well,

00:59:57.320 --> 00:59:58.153
but it was just,

00:59:58.153 --> 01:00:00.090
it was one guy in the
car and it was like a,

01:00:00.090 --> 01:00:01.730
it was a hatchback car.

01:00:01.730 --> 01:00:04.940
It could have been like a
Subaru Outback type thing

01:00:04.940 --> 01:00:07.393
that could have gone on
this off-roading part.

01:00:08.670 --> 01:00:11.530
But if you're in a car and
you go slow enough, you can,

01:00:11.530 --> 01:00:12.577
you could navigate it.

01:00:12.577 --> 01:00:15.110
And so it was just a hatchback
that's all we could tell.

01:00:15.110 --> 01:00:17.380
He was, he's leaning
from the driver's side.

01:00:17.380 --> 01:00:19.970
So she can't really see his face,

01:00:19.970 --> 01:00:21.470
but it's just some white dude.

01:00:22.500 --> 01:00:24.920
I mean, she couldn't
describe him more than that.

01:00:24.920 --> 01:00:28.047
And then he's like, she's like,

01:00:28.047 --> 01:00:29.480
"We were just wrapping up dinner."

01:00:29.480 --> 01:00:32.837
And so she said, he was like, "Okay."

01:00:32.837 --> 01:00:36.640
And he throws his hand up
in the air, like whatever.

01:00:36.640 --> 01:00:40.360
And then he slowly keeps going past us--

01:00:40.360 --> 01:00:41.193
To the other people--

01:00:41.193 --> 01:00:46.090
Down into that thing in an
up to those next people.

01:00:47.100 --> 01:00:50.973
And at that moment that
he drove away, Christy,

01:00:53.400 --> 01:00:56.070
I'm still in the kitchen,
Christy comes in there

01:00:56.070 --> 01:01:01.070
and she's visibly freaking
out and I'm also freaking out.

01:01:02.640 --> 01:01:04.790
And like, our eyes are so wide

01:01:04.790 --> 01:01:08.320
and it was like, we were
like, what just happened

01:01:08.320 --> 01:01:10.420
is what we seem to be saying to each other

01:01:10.420 --> 01:01:12.640
without actually saying words.

01:01:12.640 --> 01:01:16.753
And I was just like, she was like,

01:01:19.277 --> 01:01:20.479
"Was this guy trying to,

01:01:20.479 --> 01:01:21.312
"this guy was trying
to lure me to the car."

01:01:21.312 --> 01:01:23.237
I was like, "Yeah, I didn't
know if I should go out there

01:01:23.237 --> 01:01:24.070
"or if I should wait,

01:01:24.070 --> 01:01:25.540
"but it felt like you were handling it."

01:01:25.540 --> 01:01:27.987
And I was like, "I just didn't,

01:01:27.987 --> 01:01:28.923
"I just wanted him to go away.

01:01:28.923 --> 01:01:30.540
"And it seemed like you were
doing a good job of that."

01:01:30.540 --> 01:01:33.287
And she was like, and I was thinking,

01:01:33.287 --> 01:01:35.010
"We gotta get outta here."

01:01:35.010 --> 01:01:37.873
He's going to these,
this guy's unpredictable.

01:01:38.770 --> 01:01:39.840
He maybe unstable--

01:01:39.840 --> 01:01:41.260
Did you have a knife or anything?

01:01:41.260 --> 01:01:43.170
I wasn't thinking of that at
the time I have one of those

01:01:43.170 --> 01:01:45.320
like five and one tools
that has a knife in it.

01:01:45.320 --> 01:01:47.273
I have a giant knife.

01:01:49.334 --> 01:01:51.540
Like a hunting knife
that's like 12 inches long.

01:01:51.540 --> 01:01:53.190
And I kept it in my tent every night

01:01:53.190 --> 01:01:54.460
just in case trouble came.

01:01:54.460 --> 01:01:55.560
Yeah, yeah, well, let me tell you,

01:01:55.560 --> 01:01:57.063
I gotta rethink some things.

01:01:58.004 --> 01:01:59.160
To think things through on another level,

01:01:59.160 --> 01:02:01.320
because at this point
I'm thinking in my mind,

01:02:01.320 --> 01:02:03.670
I know Christy wants to
get the hell out of dodge.

01:02:03.670 --> 01:02:04.760
And I'm also thinking--

01:02:04.760 --> 01:02:06.720
He's got to come back
by you, right, because--

01:02:06.720 --> 01:02:08.760
We knew that he had to come back by us

01:02:08.760 --> 01:02:09.593
once he was done--

01:02:09.593 --> 01:02:11.700
Once the dad and the daughter

01:02:11.700 --> 01:02:13.270
were done judging the photos.

01:02:13.270 --> 01:02:17.360
Yes or once he's done like
killing and eating them,

01:02:17.360 --> 01:02:20.140
there is a dead end, he
has to come back by us.

01:02:20.140 --> 01:02:21.560
So we were freaking out that

01:02:22.531 --> 01:02:24.040
we knew he was coming back by.

01:02:24.040 --> 01:02:25.500
Also you still got a cell service.

01:02:25.500 --> 01:02:26.600
Did it hit you that maybe

01:02:26.600 --> 01:02:27.790
you should call the police at that point.

01:02:27.790 --> 01:02:29.560
Christy said, let's call the cops.

01:02:29.560 --> 01:02:32.067
And I'm like, "Let's
not call the cops yet,

01:02:32.067 --> 01:02:33.390
"let's not panic."

01:02:33.390 --> 01:02:37.840
And I just didn't feel like, I don't know.

01:02:37.840 --> 01:02:39.160
I just didn't wanna call the cops.

01:02:39.160 --> 01:02:41.497
We can put a, let's put a pin in that.

01:02:41.497 --> 01:02:43.490
Okay, I'm not saying that you definitively

01:02:43.490 --> 01:02:44.950
should have called the cops at that point.

01:02:44.950 --> 01:02:46.450
Christy was talking about
let's call the cops,

01:02:46.450 --> 01:02:47.890
there was a debate.

01:02:47.890 --> 01:02:50.790
There's odd, there's something
not right about this guy.

01:02:51.690 --> 01:02:53.370
There's several things
not right about this guy.

01:02:53.370 --> 01:02:55.723
So Christy was like,

01:02:57.836 --> 01:02:58.847
"You need to pack everything up

01:02:58.847 --> 01:03:01.637
"so that when he comes back
through, we can be ready.

01:03:01.637 --> 01:03:05.037
"We can be in the van,
locked up and we can,

01:03:05.037 --> 01:03:07.460
"if we need to leave, we can just leave."

01:03:07.460 --> 01:03:10.570
So I was like, listen Christy,

01:03:10.570 --> 01:03:12.990
and we turned off all
the lights in the van

01:03:12.990 --> 01:03:15.640
so that we could see
through our little window.

01:03:15.640 --> 01:03:18.870
We watched him drive down
there to those other people,

01:03:18.870 --> 01:03:19.800
with all of our lights on.

01:03:19.800 --> 01:03:22.210
We couldn't see him that
well so we're like--

01:03:22.210 --> 01:03:23.460
How easy is it to pack up?

01:03:23.460 --> 01:03:24.907
We doused everything and then I was like,

01:03:24.907 --> 01:03:27.817
"Christy, you look out at this window

01:03:27.817 --> 01:03:29.927
"and you keep your eyes glued to this guy.

01:03:29.927 --> 01:03:31.887
"If he starts coming back, you let me know

01:03:31.887 --> 01:03:35.607
"while you don't take your
eyes off of his car lights.

01:03:35.607 --> 01:03:37.540
"I'm gonna get everything cleaned up."

01:03:37.540 --> 01:03:39.970
And then I went out there and I got,

01:03:39.970 --> 01:03:41.900
the propane tank had just,

01:03:41.900 --> 01:03:44.150
propane burner had just cooled down enough

01:03:44.150 --> 01:03:47.850
to put it in the car, the
propane tank, our chairs,

01:03:47.850 --> 01:03:51.920
the cooler, I'm scrambling
putting everything away

01:03:51.920 --> 01:03:53.830
in the pitch dark without any lights on.

01:03:53.830 --> 01:03:57.370
And then I put everything
back in and I come back in

01:03:57.370 --> 01:03:59.860
and she's like, "He still there."

01:03:59.860 --> 01:04:01.430
Yeah, I mean, he's got a lot
of photos to go through."

01:04:01.430 --> 01:04:04.587
He's still there, I
don't, you know, did he,

01:04:04.587 --> 01:04:06.030
did he kill both of them?

01:04:06.030 --> 01:04:07.960
I don't know, what's he doing?

01:04:07.960 --> 01:04:10.723
Is he putting on their skin as a suit?

01:04:11.950 --> 01:04:15.127
I don't know what's happening,
but I'm thinking if we,

01:04:15.127 --> 01:04:17.287
and I asked Christie, this is like,

01:04:17.287 --> 01:04:20.417
"If we're watching a
movie of us right now,

01:04:20.417 --> 01:04:23.827
"what would we be saying
to our characters?

01:04:23.827 --> 01:04:25.730
"Get the hell out of here."

01:04:25.730 --> 01:04:26.900
Yeah, but in the movie that

01:04:26.900 --> 01:04:29.110
you would definitely have judged
the photos because of what,

01:04:29.110 --> 01:04:32.740
I mean, that's what would
be more fun for a plot.

01:04:32.740 --> 01:04:35.310
Well, really, let me see your photos.

01:04:35.310 --> 01:04:37.750
Christy would have, Christy
did stand up I think,

01:04:37.750 --> 01:04:40.603
but she did not walk towards
the man with the photos.

01:04:41.610 --> 01:04:44.411
We knew he was coming back and we're like,

01:04:44.411 --> 01:04:45.570
I don't wanna be the people in the movie

01:04:45.570 --> 01:04:46.810
that I'm gonna be angry at.

01:04:46.810 --> 01:04:47.840
We need to be ready to leave.

01:04:47.840 --> 01:04:50.880
So like we locked up the
van, we locked up everything.

01:04:50.880 --> 01:04:55.880
And then all of a sudden
that the car starts moving

01:04:56.400 --> 01:04:57.740
and it starts creeping back.

01:04:57.740 --> 01:05:01.390
And because of the terrain,
it had to go so slow.

01:05:01.390 --> 01:05:04.520
And it went down in
that berm and it came up

01:05:04.520 --> 01:05:06.990
and we're looking out the
back two windows of the van

01:05:06.990 --> 01:05:09.370
where he would drive right past us.

01:05:09.370 --> 01:05:14.280
And he drives and he gets,
comes right up to the van

01:05:16.530 --> 01:05:20.770
and then keeps going slowly.

01:05:20.770 --> 01:05:22.770
And he goes down below the van

01:05:22.770 --> 01:05:24.197
and he gets back to the paved road

01:05:24.197 --> 01:05:25.320
and we could still see him.

01:05:25.320 --> 01:05:28.910
And he stops there at the
paved road and he doesn't,

01:05:28.910 --> 01:05:31.230
he has to turn right or left.

01:05:31.230 --> 01:05:32.450
He doesn't turn anywhere.

01:05:32.450 --> 01:05:35.863
He sits there for a
long time and I'm like--

01:05:35.863 --> 01:05:36.740
Like how long?

01:05:36.740 --> 01:05:38.800
It felt like 10 minutes.

01:05:38.800 --> 01:05:41.680
Like he was like, I don't
know, what is he blocking

01:05:41.680 --> 01:05:43.410
our only exit.

01:05:43.410 --> 01:05:46.930
Like we're cowering in this van locked up.

01:05:46.930 --> 01:05:48.680
And then he turns left

01:05:49.570 --> 01:05:52.470
and we like watch him
go down into the canyon.

01:05:52.470 --> 01:05:55.270
And then we watched him
go up on another berm

01:05:55.270 --> 01:05:56.640
where a long ways away,

01:05:56.640 --> 01:05:59.093
we saw that there was
another camper and it's like,

01:06:00.117 --> 01:06:01.860
Christy is like, "We
need to get out of here."

01:06:01.860 --> 01:06:06.860
And it was like, she was
like, you've, you can't drive.

01:06:08.300 --> 01:06:10.980
It's like, "You don't wanna get a DUI."

01:06:10.980 --> 01:06:12.310
She didn't want her first experience

01:06:12.310 --> 01:06:14.743
driving the sprinter
